1
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,740
Long ago, Gold Roger,

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:08,457
the King of Pirates, obtained
everything the world had to offer,

3
00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,940
and his dying roads drove
countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,040
You can have it!

6
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,700
I left everything in one place.

7
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:19,940
Now you just have to find it!

8
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:21,800
And thus a new age began.

9
00:00:22,080 --> 00:00:25,380
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,457
Oh, I'm done playing
through with the waiting.

11
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:31,377
Either way, I'm feeling alive!

12
00:00:31,460 --> 00:00:32,860
Look out below.

13
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,100
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

14
00:00:38,860 --> 00:00:40,397
Raise your flag up high.

15
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:43,040
Hail a brand new dawn.

16
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:45,837
Blaze across the sky.

17
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,837
Time to journey on.

18
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,317
On your mark.

19
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,197
Camel of other things.

20
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,137
We're on Earth, a legendary.

21
00:00:53,220 --> 00:00:54,050
Hooray!

22
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:57,600
If you can show your breath,
Then we'll make some waves.

23
00:00:58,880 --> 00:01:00,377
We run our daunted.

24
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:01,637
Ain't no beginners.

25
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:04,357
Cause if you're wanted,
Then you're a winner.

26
00:01:04,440 --> 00:01:09,840
For we are on the cruise,
And freedom is the only rule.

27
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:12,277
Fearless night and day.

28
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:14,140
Cause that's just our way.

29
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:17,197
Find one piece.

30
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:18,537
I'll be the first.

31
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:19,797
I've heard it be so bad.

32
00:01:19,880 --> 00:01:20,710
I could burst.

33
00:01:20,793 --> 00:01:22,137
It's all this real.

34
00:01:22,220 --> 00:01:26,277
It must be cause my hand's on a wheel.

35
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:29,457
I'm done playing, feel it's waiting.

36
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:31,457
In a world I'm feeling alive.

37
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:33,237
But I'll be loud.

38
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:37,040
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

39
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:40,500
We have come so far.

40
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:44,320
Gotta make it to the end.

41
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:47,677
Whatever danger we find,
no one ever left behind!

42
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:50,820
I've always got your back, my friend.

43
00:01:52,580 --> 00:01:55,457
Sail on shoreward, keep marching forward.

44
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:59,097
Dreaming from the very
first day I'd make my name.

45
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:03,120
And don't you know that
dream hasn't changed?

46
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:06,317
I'm done playing through with the wave.

47
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:08,297
In every world I'm feeling alive.

48
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,640
Look out below.

49
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:12,980
Wake up, sunshine.

50
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:17,057
Wake up, sunshine.

51
00:02:17,140 --> 00:02:23,560
Wake up, sunshine, here we go!

52
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:28,340
We go.

53
00:02:49,640 --> 00:02:52,437
Those officers were like
demons straight out of hell.

54
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:55,037
But they were a joke to the Straw Hats.

55
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:57,300
I'm glad they're on our side.

56
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:31,100
Heads up, fish people!

57
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:32,660
Eyes on the sky!

58
00:03:32,940 --> 00:03:34,411
Danger's on the way down!

59
00:03:38,040 --> 00:03:39,640
It's one on Sabo!

60
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:41,300
Those fours are flat!

61
00:03:56,100 --> 00:03:59,137
Could have dropped him in a
place with less people, dumbass.

62
00:03:59,220 --> 00:04:00,050
Shut it!

63
00:04:00,133 --> 00:04:03,138
Keep complaining and I'll
drop the next giant on you!

64
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:10,940
That was downright amazing, Sanji!

65
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,560
Hey Chopper, you mind shrinking down some?

66
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:20,917
You're totally upstaging
my giant robot here.

67
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,577
Franky, that beam was so cool!

68
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:25,000
Are you serious?

69
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:27,144
That robot was utterly useless.

70
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:31,257
That reminds me.

71
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:32,170
Nami?

72
00:04:32,253 --> 00:04:33,420
What is it?

73
00:04:34,280 --> 00:04:36,297
You should really wear a miniskirt.

74
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,210
Stop it!

75
00:04:37,293 --> 00:04:38,868
I can't really read my dad?

76
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:43,520
Well done.

77
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,859
Expected no less from Luffy's crew.

78
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:47,830
Wait.

79
00:04:48,660 --> 00:04:49,880
There's an Owa!

80
00:05:00,260 --> 00:05:02,780
The Owa's right above us!

81
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,557
It's gonna crush every last one of us.

82
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:14,297
We gotta get out of here!

83
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:16,597
Neptune's army might trap us in the plaza.

84
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:17,510
If we don't?

85
00:05:17,593 --> 00:05:18,423
We can make it!

86
00:05:18,506 --> 00:05:20,633
Those psycho officers can't stop us now.

87
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:22,540
Are you okay?

88
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,340
Oh no, are we too late?

89
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:32,900
Please do something Stop that thing!

90
00:05:34,020 --> 00:05:35,280
Straw Hat!

91
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,520
Straw Hat is still fighting!

92
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:51,600
He's not giving up yet!

93
00:05:55,640 --> 00:05:57,816
I can hardly believe what I'm seeing!

94
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:05,440
He still has strength length!

95
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,420
He's attacking the Noah!

96
00:06:11,260 --> 00:06:12,920
It's breaking apart!

97
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:23,937
We'll be alright if he can
obliterate it before it crashes,

98
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:28,197
but if he's unable to,
then we're all doomed!

99
00:06:28,280 --> 00:06:32,060
It will be the end for Fishman Island.

100
00:06:32,460 --> 00:06:35,000
Give it everything you got, Lupi!

101
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:37,897
You got it!

102
00:06:37,980 --> 00:06:39,039
Are you down here?

103
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:41,260
Come on, you can do it!

104
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,240
I believe in you.

105
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:59,037
Make it happen, Straw Hat!

106
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,677
We're rooting for you down here!

107
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:02,037
We know you can do it!

108
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,957
Keep it up, Straw Hat!

109
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:07,217
You may be a human but you've
got all of our support!

110
00:07:07,300 --> 00:07:08,771
We ain't running nowhere!

111
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,980
Go Straw Hacks!

112
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:12,820
We all believe in you!

113
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:17,680
We save our country, Straw Hacks!

114
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:18,880
Save us all!

115
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:21,120
Tear it apart, Straw Hacks!

116
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,380
We don't need that ship anymore!

117
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:36,880
Straw Hacks!

118
00:07:37,840 --> 00:07:38,670
No!

119
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:39,770
Snowhead!

120
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:40,690
Snowhead!

121
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,760
Snowhead! Snowhead!

122
00:07:44,040 --> 00:07:45,300
Stop that tower!

123
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:46,580
Destroy it!

124
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:47,980
Terror it to bits!

125
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:49,620
Wreck it all!

126
00:07:58,040 --> 00:07:59,240
Wait, Lucy!

127
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:06,120
The moon is opening up again! J-Box!

128
00:08:07,580 --> 00:08:08,800
You want to help?

129
00:08:08,980 --> 00:08:10,156
Stay back and watch!

130
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:13,789
All that matters now with speed,
carry the damn thing apart!

131
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,980
Stop, you dumb shit!

132
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:21,660
Stop falling!

133
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,980
I'm sorry that this had to happen, Father.

134
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:37,577
Destroying the Noah?

135
00:08:37,660 --> 00:08:40,280
It's the only thing to be done.

136
00:08:42,780 --> 00:08:44,897
We're losing the ship of promise!

137
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:46,460
But what can be done?

138
00:08:47,100 --> 00:08:49,057
My people's lives are more important.

139
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:50,937
Still, I'm sorry.

140
00:08:51,020 --> 00:08:53,557
I'm sorry that I cannot keep the promise.

141
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:54,920
Joy Boy!

142
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,240
You may stop.

143
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:04,160
Who's there?

144
00:09:08,900 --> 00:09:10,100
Enough, Luffy!

145
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,460
You can't do this!

146
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,800
You have to stop!

147
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,925
You're going to kill yourself!

148
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,900
Move with me, Hachi!

149
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,860
I have to save the island!

150
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,420
It's so tight now!

151
00:09:24,840 --> 00:09:25,840
It's not alright!

152
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,137
Everyone's gonna die if I don't!

153
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:29,338
Will you just look?

154
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:31,320
The Noah stopped!

155
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:45,340
The sea kinks, but why?

156
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:50,460
You're angry!

157
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:52,780
I don't like it when you yell at me!

158
00:09:53,540 --> 00:09:54,370
Hey!

159
00:09:54,453 --> 00:09:56,454
We've got bigger problems to deal with!

160
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:04,149
I don't know what this means,
but I think it's a good thing.

161
00:10:04,660 --> 00:10:05,620
They stopped it.

162
00:10:06,020 --> 00:10:08,140
Somehow, the Noah's not falling.

163
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,080
What in the hell is happening?

164
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:16,596
Are you seeing this?

165
00:10:17,020 --> 00:10:19,432
Did the Sea King seriously stop the Noah?

166
00:10:25,380 --> 00:10:26,460
Oh, Luffy!

167
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:29,197
You're losing so much
blood from that wound!

168
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:31,104
We need to get you to a doctor!

169
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:40,380
Yeah, well, it's okay, really.

170
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:44,777
Just as long as the ship is stopped.

171
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:49,760
I'm just glad everyone is safe now.

172
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:52,940
Help me!

173
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:56,240
He'll be alright.

174
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:09,140
I gotta admit, that there
is one hell of a human.

175
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:13,000
Yeah, to say the least, he
sure is strong, isn't he?

176
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:17,557
Even if we had been late, the
island would have been saved,

177
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:21,287
at the cost of the Noah being
completely destroyed, of course.

178
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:26,897
Well, it's a good thing
we did make it then.

179
00:11:26,980 --> 00:11:32,280
I sure am glad that Princess Shirahoshi
called out to us like that, just in time.

180
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:36,280
But I didn't do anything at all.

181
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,620
I was just sad.

182
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,510
Not quite.

183
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:43,897
Your will and the will of the human
echoed as one becoming a wish.

184
00:11:43,980 --> 00:11:45,680
A prayer to us.

185
00:11:49,900 --> 00:11:55,277
Your desire to save your people was so
strong, and we all heard it loud and clear.

186
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:57,960
You're not nearly as
helpless as you think.

187
00:12:13,020 --> 00:12:17,360
The power of the Sea
Kingdoms is yours as well.

188
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:21,560
If you are in need, then
we shall heed your call.

189
00:12:31,080 --> 00:12:32,580
People of the Kingdom.

190
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:35,700
I'm not sure what just happened here.

191
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:38,254
I'm not even sure if I can describe it.

192
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:41,620
But, whatever it was, it happened.

193
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,740
The Noah, it's been stopped!

194
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:51,460
And it's damaged, but not destroyed.

195
00:12:54,500 --> 00:12:57,820
Frishman Island has been saved!

196
00:12:59,300 --> 00:13:01,660
I knew Straw Hat would save us!

197
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:07,640
Thank you.

198
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:35,257
Princess Shirahoshi,

199
00:13:35,340 --> 00:13:40,164
you can't imagine how long we see kings
waited for you to be born into this world.

200
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,040
Waited for me?

201
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:46,180
This vessel was designed for
us to pull it, can't you tell?

202
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:52,220
This responsibility has been passed
down for as long as anyone can remember.

203
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:55,397
Then, is that the reason
why the Noah is so large?

204
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:56,720
Worse.

205
00:13:57,100 --> 00:14:00,120
Our queen appears once
every several centuries,

206
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:04,224
though we do not know why she
always takes the form of a mermaid.

207
00:14:04,600 --> 00:14:05,560
It's strange.

208
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:09,017
I wonder.

209
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:12,697
But we do know that ever
since you were born,

210
00:14:12,780 --> 00:14:16,980
you have been our exalted queen.

211
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:24,300
Is she? Yes.

212
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:27,477
I don't understand it, but I think...

213
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:30,520
Our sister is speaking with the Sea Kings.

214
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,430
Incredible.

215
00:14:32,680 --> 00:14:34,157
You're not going to believe this, sir,

216
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:37,877
but a bunch of Sea Kings just showed up
out of the blue and they took hold of it.

217
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:41,195
And I'm not sure I understand
what they're saying, sir.

218
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:43,357
But I guess they stepped
in because they wanted

219
00:14:43,440 --> 00:14:46,205
to stop Luffy from smashing
the Noah to pieces.

220
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:50,459
For whatever reason, that shit must
be really important to them, too.

221
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:51,940
Your Majesty.

222
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,350
Hmm.

223
00:14:56,433 --> 00:14:57,517
Sea kings.

224
00:14:57,600 --> 00:15:00,120
So, it's finally awakened.

225
00:15:00,560 --> 00:15:04,140
The power that can
destroy this entire world.

226
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:06,780
Look!

227
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:11,400
The bubble's being absorbed
by the island bit by bit.

228
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:14,100
He won't survive in the deep sea.

229
00:15:14,920 --> 00:15:16,340
Quickly, Shirahoshi.

230
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:18,380
You must retrieve him.

231
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:36,457
if i didn't know better i'd
say that the human wearing

232
00:15:36,540 --> 00:15:41,060
the hat was able to hear
us as well I doubt that.

233
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,180
It has happened before.

234
00:15:44,740 --> 00:15:46,520
Not so long ago.

235
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,780
Oh, I remember.

236
00:15:51,560 --> 00:15:54,089
Rayleigh, did you hear
that voice just now?

237
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:55,700
You're crazy.

238
00:15:56,020 --> 00:15:58,079
There's obviously nobody down here.

239
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,500
Who's there?

240
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:04,053
Why am I hearing strange voices
at the bottom of the sea?

241
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:06,440
Show yourself now!

242
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,200
Quite mysterious.

243
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,700
Quite mysterious indeed.

244
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:22,770
Ah!

245
00:16:22,853 --> 00:16:24,020
Seeking's you!

246
00:16:24,460 --> 00:16:26,680
And they're pulling the Noah! Ah!

247
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:28,340
Please don't eat me!

248
00:16:33,180 --> 00:16:35,400
The Noah is crumbling.

249
00:16:36,160 --> 00:16:38,000
Can it be saved?

250
00:16:39,160 --> 00:16:41,040
Can it serve its purpose?

251
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:47,740
Well, I believe it could be
saved if we had their help.

252
00:16:48,900 --> 00:16:51,600
However, this is a different age.

253
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:55,440
Then can it be repaired?

254
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:57,720
I certainly hope so.

255
00:16:58,500 --> 00:17:01,100
The appointed time is approaching.

256
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:11,574
Minister of the Left, sir, we have a
report from inside the Ryugu palace.

257
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:12,570
What's happening?

258
00:17:12,653 --> 00:17:15,457
Well, the good news is we've located
all the mermaids who were kidnapped.

259
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,497
It turns out they're right
here on the premises.

260
00:17:17,580 --> 00:17:18,957
Oh, thank goodness!

261
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:21,340
Please tell me they're all right.

262
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,717
Yes, they said they're still
feeling a bit disoriented,

263
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:28,697
sir, but they do remember
what the culprit looked like.

264
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:33,057
Bad news is the treasure
chamber's been wiped clean.

265
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:36,377
They took it all down to the last piece.

266
00:17:36,460 --> 00:17:38,137
It's awful.

267
00:17:38,220 --> 00:17:40,517
We even lost the tomate box, sir.

268
00:17:40,600 --> 00:17:44,397
Your Majesty,

269
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:48,177
someone seems to have robbed
us during the commotion.

270
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:50,857
Stolen treasures do not concern us.

271
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:55,117
Now, not moments ago, we
nearly lost our entire kingdom.

272
00:17:55,200 --> 00:18:00,197
The best thing to do at present is tell

273
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:02,637
the citizens that the mermaids are safe.

274
00:18:02,720 --> 00:18:08,037
The damage may be done, but we still
need to clear the Straw Hats' names.

275
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:11,077
We must do the right thing.

276
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:17,697
I won't hesitate to shoot

277
00:18:17,780 --> 00:18:18,997
you if you try to get a worm.

278
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:20,317
Am I clear?

279
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,837
Never mind.

280
00:18:22,920 --> 00:18:24,757
You're gonna kill us boss team day.

281
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:25,677
Come on, please.

282
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,717
You gotta let us out of
here We only did this

283
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,757
stuff cuz we were scared
of holding in his crib.

284
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:33,937
We are humans You know this fish man
civil war things got nothing to do

285
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:38,720
with us besides tourism from human
pirates is good for their economy So, uh,

286
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:39,797
yeah, come on man.

287
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:44,660
Just let us go, please the punishment
may not be as terrible as you think

288
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:49,080
Let us wait to hear the
royal family's decision.

289
00:18:51,540 --> 00:18:54,657
There is one fact of which we must make

290
00:18:54,740 --> 00:18:58,937
all of you aware the mermaids are safe.

291
00:18:59,020 --> 00:19:03,320
And as for the Straw Hats they
were not involved in any way.

292
00:19:05,580 --> 00:19:09,217
We humbly admit that
mistakes were made in our

293
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:12,597
investigation for the
unrest that this has caused.

294
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:18,120
We must apologize you know i never
doubted the Straw Hats for a second.

295
00:19:18,820 --> 00:19:20,697
I knew it wasn't them from the start.

296
00:19:20,780 --> 00:19:22,157
I just didn't want to say anything.

297
00:19:22,240 --> 00:19:23,070
Drop the app.

298
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:25,560
We're all to blame. Look at us.

299
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,720
We didn't trust them for a second.

300
00:19:28,960 --> 00:19:31,940
Nah, we believed them
all along, right? Yeah.

301
00:19:32,160 --> 00:19:33,377
Hey, that's not true.

302
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:34,360
Don't say that.

303
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:36,560
I heard what you said. Me too.

304
00:19:38,860 --> 00:19:39,690
Admit it.

305
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,824
We all believed the Straw
Hats were responsible.

306
00:19:43,040 --> 00:19:44,200
We judged them.

307
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:46,485
Just because they were humans.

308
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:49,238
Yeah, you're right.

309
00:19:49,340 --> 00:19:50,987
We've always been like that.

310
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,160
I feel awful.

311
00:19:54,720 --> 00:19:55,550
Super!

312
00:19:58,640 --> 00:19:59,920
Look at that!

313
00:20:00,100 --> 00:20:01,197
It's just like mine!

314
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:02,339
Yeah, only cooler!

315
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:05,217
It's because I use
Monster Point, that's all.

316
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,577
That one wears me out.

317
00:20:06,660 --> 00:20:12,060
I won't be able to walk for a few hours,
but I can still treat your injuries,

318
00:20:12,260 --> 00:20:13,090
slowly.

319
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:15,437
Now those hurt, let me take a look.

320
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:16,817
Worry about yourself first.

321
00:20:16,900 --> 00:20:21,560
It looks like everyone here is fine
except for me after all that fighting.

322
00:20:21,700 --> 00:20:25,288
I need to rest my head, too Only
your lap can heal me, please

323
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:30,160
Rest it up your ass instead
if Robin wants me to what?

324
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:32,010
Luffy

325
00:20:32,660 --> 00:20:34,260
The Princes are here!

326
00:20:41,460 --> 00:20:43,500
It's Hordean Deccan!

327
00:20:43,800 --> 00:20:44,840
We've returned.

328
00:20:45,340 --> 00:20:47,400
We're sorry we worried you, father.

329
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:50,036
All that matters is that you're safe.

330
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,010
Hear me, citizens!

331
00:20:57,093 --> 00:20:58,580
There is no need to fear!

332
00:20:59,280 --> 00:21:02,927
Never again will these villains
cause trouble for our kingdom!

333
00:21:05,840 --> 00:21:06,670
Whoa!

334
00:21:06,780 --> 00:21:08,780
Has this been a crazy day or what?

335
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:12,320
What a terrible monster that is!

336
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:15,480
And to think he was right
here in our neighborhood.

337
00:21:16,820 --> 00:21:19,920
Captain Horton, what happened to you?

338
00:21:22,820 --> 00:21:24,920
We shouted who's boss!

339
00:21:28,580 --> 00:21:29,410
Huh?

340
00:21:29,493 --> 00:21:30,323
I know that voice.

341
00:21:31,060 --> 00:21:32,057
That's the princess!

342
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:33,360
Seems she's okay!

343
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:36,428
Look, it's the princess
and Straw Hat Luffy!

344
00:21:37,060 --> 00:21:38,060
Someone help!

345
00:21:38,180 --> 00:21:39,417
I don't know what to do!

346
00:21:39,500 --> 00:21:41,324
I hope you won't stop bleeding!

347
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:43,560
I'm afraid he's going to die!

348
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:49,460
Luffy's so brave, he could've
died out there, fighting for us!

349
00:21:49,780 --> 00:21:50,740
Hope he's okay.

350
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:55,700
This looks bad, but I've got a
few hemostatics here in my bag.

351
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:59,137
Thanks a lot, Robin? Sure!

352
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:02,660
Whoa, is that new form really
worth doing this every time?

353
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:04,660
Right, here we go.

354
00:22:05,780 --> 00:22:07,077
Let me help you, Moon.

355
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:07,990
What?

356
00:22:08,073 --> 00:22:09,340
What kind of doctor are you?

357
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:10,897
A little left, there.

358
00:22:10,980 --> 00:22:13,877
Oh, doctor, tell me Luffy's
going to be alright?

359
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:17,607
He can stop the bleeding, but
he's lost an awful lot of blood.

360
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,600
He needs a donor.

361
00:22:20,460 --> 00:22:21,837
Well, that's no good.

362
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:23,697
Luffy's the only one of us with type F.

363
00:22:23,780 --> 00:22:24,877
So we can't do it?

364
00:22:24,960 --> 00:22:26,960
There's got to be someone who can.

365
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:28,450
Somebody!

366
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:29,460
Help us!

367
00:22:30,160 --> 00:22:31,440
I'm type F.

368
00:22:31,600 --> 00:22:33,717
I'm the right type, but...

369
00:22:33,800 --> 00:22:35,760
Papa, you're type F, right?

370
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:37,997
Well, I, uh...

371
00:22:38,080 --> 00:22:39,060
Oh, right!

372
00:22:39,220 --> 00:22:43,437
I forgot in this country there's actually
a law against donating blood to humans.

373
00:22:43,520 --> 00:22:44,350
What?

374
00:22:44,433 --> 00:22:46,480
What kind of law is that? It's cruel.

375
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:48,600
Aw, come on!

376
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:50,320
This guy just saved you!

377
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:54,997
I'd like to help but I'm afraid
my blood isn't tight enough.

378
00:22:55,080 --> 00:22:56,517
It is red though!

379
00:22:56,600 --> 00:22:58,120
Is that good enough?

380
00:22:58,540 --> 00:23:00,837
That's not really how it works but thanks.

381
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:03,937
Princess Shiromoshi Wait a sec.

382
00:23:04,020 --> 00:23:06,380
Maybe the human pirates could help it.

383
00:23:15,360 --> 00:23:18,260
You can give him some of my blood.

384
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:21,217
It's type f.

385
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:23,457
Take as much as you need.

386
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:24,370
Wow.

387
00:23:24,453 --> 00:23:25,977
Really thanks, Jimbae!

388
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:28,017
Wait but the law...

389
00:23:28,100 --> 00:23:29,377
what of it?

390
00:23:29,460 --> 00:23:32,857
I'm a pirate boss, Jimbae.

391
00:23:32,940 --> 00:23:35,577
You're the boss, Jimbae!

392
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:36,537
Wonderful!

393
00:23:36,620 --> 00:23:39,357
Wait, Jimbae!

394
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,270
If you...

395
00:23:40,353 --> 00:23:41,477
it's all right.

396
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:45,680
What makes it so wrong?

397
00:23:46,020 --> 00:23:51,520
It's precisely that kind of thinking
that caused this to begin with.

398
00:24:11,680 --> 00:24:13,640
It might sting a little, okay?

399
00:24:14,300 --> 00:24:15,480
I can take it.

400
00:24:37,580 --> 00:24:39,740
If you harm someone...

401
00:24:47,940 --> 00:24:48,860
Or,

402
00:24:49,100 --> 00:24:50,740
if someone harms you,

403
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:56,937
the same red

404
00:24:57,020 --> 00:24:58,420
blood is spilled.

405
00:25:08,900 --> 00:25:12,420
And this tube through
which that blood flows,

406
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:16,160
small and fragile though it is,

407
00:25:16,660 --> 00:25:18,260
provides a pathway,

408
00:25:18,660 --> 00:25:25,557
through

409
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,470
the prejudice

410
00:25:26,553 --> 00:25:28,157
that divides us,

411
00:25:28,240 --> 00:25:35,240
and

412
00:25:40,180 --> 00:25:41,010
the

413
00:25:41,093 --> 00:25:41,923
conflicts

414
00:25:42,006 --> 00:25:42,836
that we create.

415
00:25:48,280 --> 00:25:51,000
as though they were never there at all.

416
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:57,280
And more than any fleeting
dream or fantasy could,

417
00:25:57,580 --> 00:26:00,080
this path can guide us to the surface?

418
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:02,660
into the warm light of the sun.

419
00:26:15,920 --> 00:26:21,697
Team Bay Luffy It scared me.

420
00:26:21,780 --> 00:26:22,610
Luffy

421
00:26:24,240 --> 00:26:26,357
You rascal!

422
00:26:26,440 --> 00:26:28,720
So you were awake?

423
00:26:31,760 --> 00:26:33,200
He's okay!

424
00:26:33,780 --> 00:26:34,940
Yay, Reef!

425
00:27:02,560 --> 00:27:04,160
You see, mother?

426
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,740
We made it.

427
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:11,580
Back to Saru.

428
00:27:26,020 --> 00:27:27,660
Hey, Zunbei.

429
00:27:39,520 --> 00:27:43,080
I want you to join my crew.

430
00:27:44,780 --> 00:27:47,160
The royal family has reached a decision!

431
00:27:50,220 --> 00:27:51,060
Freak up!

432
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:52,120
Finally free!

433
00:27:52,660 --> 00:27:54,040
Screw you, Wardy!

434
00:27:54,240 --> 00:27:55,416
Now who's in chains?

435
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:59,577
Sorry that I was going to be a
slave for the rest of my life.

436
00:27:59,660 --> 00:28:00,717
Thank you, Straw Hats.

437
00:28:00,800 --> 00:28:02,617
I swear I'll repay you someday!

438
00:28:02,700 --> 00:28:05,860
After I become king of the pirates? What?

439
00:28:06,340 --> 00:28:09,297
That's a bit ambitious Hey,
what's wrong with having trees?

440
00:28:09,380 --> 00:28:12,260
Oh, pirates, I can set
sail for the new world?

441
00:28:13,460 --> 00:28:17,460
Your majesty Are you sure it's wise
to release Hody's human slaves?

442
00:28:17,700 --> 00:28:20,637
We can't let such fears turn
us into something we're not.

443
00:28:20,720 --> 00:28:24,897
This island has always been a welcoming,
safe place for pirates to rest.

444
00:28:24,980 --> 00:28:27,777
And these humans never meant
us any deliberate harm.

445
00:28:27,860 --> 00:28:30,237
We have no right to imprison them.

446
00:28:30,320 --> 00:28:33,577
Now then, as for the rest
of the new Fishman Pirates?

447
00:28:33,660 --> 00:28:35,340
That's a different story.

448
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,417
Don't cut my head off!

449
00:28:37,500 --> 00:28:39,157
Please bear our lives.

450
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:40,497
Your Highness, really?

451
00:28:40,580 --> 00:28:42,997
We didn't know anything about
Heart killing the Queen.

452
00:28:43,080 --> 00:28:44,117
They lied to us.

453
00:28:44,200 --> 00:28:46,357
We got duped by a bunch of lunatics.

454
00:28:46,440 --> 00:28:47,270
That's the truth!

455
00:28:47,353 --> 00:28:48,317
It's Horty's fault.

456
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:49,997
We're not responsible.

457
00:28:50,080 --> 00:28:51,840
From here on?

458
00:28:52,540 --> 00:28:56,040
I officially order you all to
live here on the main island.

459
00:28:58,220 --> 00:28:59,060
Hang on!

460
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:01,457
You're telling us to
live law-abiding lives?

461
00:29:01,540 --> 00:29:04,537
It could be a lot worse,
better than working for Heart.

462
00:29:04,620 --> 00:29:05,450
Come on!

463
00:29:05,533 --> 00:29:06,737
You can't be serious, King!

464
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:08,879
We don't want them living among us!

465
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:12,294
We won't feel safe to let our
kids walk down the street!

466
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,200
To clarify,

467
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,497
you will serve your time, of course,

468
00:29:16,580 --> 00:29:18,897
and you will work under
the supervision of my army.

469
00:29:18,980 --> 00:29:24,040
I will provide you all with gainful
employment to use up all that energy of yours.

470
00:29:24,260 --> 00:29:26,040
And from this day forward,

471
00:29:26,240 --> 00:29:30,140
the Fishman District will be sealed
off and all entry prohibited.

472
00:29:32,020 --> 00:29:35,140
The dark side of the
Fishman had been exposed,

473
00:29:35,380 --> 00:29:38,040
along with the true
killer of Queen Otohime.

474
00:29:39,120 --> 00:29:44,180
The conspirator, Heart Jones, attempted
to seize control of Fishman Island.

475
00:29:44,860 --> 00:29:46,220
But he failed.

476
00:29:46,520 --> 00:29:49,197
All thanks to a band of
human pirates who happened

477
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,927
to be passing through
at just the right time.

478
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:55,820
Hey, have you seen Straw Hat Luffy around?

479
00:29:57,440 --> 00:29:59,540
Well, he, um, absconded.

480
00:30:00,340 --> 00:30:03,277
Why did you leave the plaza
without saying anything?

481
00:30:03,360 --> 00:30:04,595
Are you running away?

482
00:30:04,920 --> 00:30:06,780
We're not too big on attention.

483
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:10,777
You saw how many spectators we
had watching us fight down there.

484
00:30:10,860 --> 00:30:14,957
If we stick around, they'd just treat
us like heroes or some dumb crap.

485
00:30:15,040 --> 00:30:17,687
Just the thought of it
makes me want to puke.

486
00:30:17,780 --> 00:30:18,610
But why?

487
00:30:18,700 --> 00:30:21,257
Isn't it a good thing to
be the hero of a nation?

488
00:30:21,340 --> 00:30:22,170
Listen up.

489
00:30:22,253 --> 00:30:23,477
I'll spell it out for you.

490
00:30:23,560 --> 00:30:27,266
A man who shares his sake with
other people, now that's a hero.

491
00:30:27,580 --> 00:30:29,400
But I want it all for myself.

492
00:30:29,760 --> 00:30:30,940
Keep your damn sake!

493
00:30:31,140 --> 00:30:33,197
And stop putting dumb ideas in her head!

494
00:30:33,280 --> 00:30:35,097
Why won't you join us, Deep Bay?

495
00:30:35,180 --> 00:30:37,157
I know you've got adventure in your blood!

496
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:39,577
Come on, it'll be the most
fun you've ever had, I swear!

497
00:30:39,660 --> 00:30:40,500
He's right!

498
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:41,974
Crew up with us, boss!

499
00:30:42,500 --> 00:30:45,137
It'd be awesome to have
a former warlord with us!

500
00:30:45,220 --> 00:30:46,160
And helpful!

501
00:30:46,560 --> 00:30:48,442
Luffy could take a little break!

502
00:30:49,660 --> 00:30:53,060
I told you, it's impossible
for me to join you now.

503
00:30:54,140 --> 00:30:55,600
But I am still grateful.

504
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:57,685
It is an honor that you asked.

505
00:30:58,360 --> 00:31:03,197
I am certain that it would be the adventure
of my life to sail the sea with you all.

506
00:31:03,280 --> 00:31:06,957
But I am afraid I don't have the
luxury to indulge in such pleasures.

507
00:31:07,040 --> 00:31:10,517
I have responsibilities
that I must fulfill.

508
00:31:10,600 --> 00:31:13,700
And I put them off long enough as it is.

509
00:31:14,660 --> 00:31:16,717
Once I've seen, to my duties.

510
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:19,820
When I'm free from my sworn obligations.

511
00:31:20,560 --> 00:31:23,457
I promise I'll set sail and seek you out!

512
00:31:23,540 --> 00:31:25,160
No matter where you may be.

513
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:28,577
And if you haven't changed your mind.

514
00:31:28,660 --> 00:31:31,337
And still wish for me to
become a member of your crew.

515
00:31:31,420 --> 00:31:34,437
Well, I'll gladly take
you up on your offer then.

516
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:36,397
If you see fit to have me?

517
00:31:36,480 --> 00:31:38,186
You better keep that promise.

518
00:31:43,020 --> 00:31:43,900
Whoa, hey.

519
00:31:44,340 --> 00:31:46,377
A man's got to do what a man's got to do.

520
00:31:46,460 --> 00:31:48,077
Give him some time, Captain.

521
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:50,101
He's really taken with Jean-Bang.

522
00:31:56,420 --> 00:31:58,717
Luffy made it clear you're worth the wait.

523
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:01,540
So if you need some me time, you got it.

524
00:32:02,160 --> 00:32:04,320
That is very gracious of you.

525
00:32:05,060 --> 00:32:07,640
So what are we doing next? Where to?

526
00:32:07,920 --> 00:32:09,038
A new world, right?

527
00:32:10,580 --> 00:32:11,410
What?

528
00:32:11,493 --> 00:32:12,837
You're leaving just like that?

529
00:32:12,920 --> 00:32:14,577
I haven't thanked you properly.

530
00:32:14,660 --> 00:32:15,880
It's not fair.

531
00:32:16,220 --> 00:32:18,102
Why, we've hardly spoken at all.

532
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:20,120
Okay, it's settled then.

533
00:32:20,360 --> 00:32:22,757
Let's stay at the Mermaid
Cafe a whole week.

534
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:25,311
